  "notes": "fiat-crypto: Coq repo for cryptographic primitive synthesis. Uses heavy tactic automation: fsatz (field arithmetic), Z.zero_bounds (zero bounds), break_match/break_innermost_match (case splitting), destruct_head (head destruct), distr_length (list length automation), straightline/straightline_call (bedrock2 separation logic). Commit messages: Bump X from Y to Z (#PR) = submodule update; 'Ed25519: ...' / 'Edwards25519: ...' = proof work on curve; 'Adapt to coq/coq#N' = spec_change adapting to upstream. Most proof work lacks explicit 'proof' keyword in subject. Admitted/admit markers occur in bedrock2 section (separation logic proofs). PR numbers appear as (#NNNN) suffix.",
